# LF in the repository and LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# molt is Windows-correct from day one, and that cuts both ways: the tool writes changeset files,
# changelogs and pyproject edits with LF regardless of host (research doc 02 section 12.6), and the
# repository storing it has to do the same. Without this, `core.autocrlf` decides -- so the same
# file lands CRLF for a Windows contributor and LF for everyone else, and a byte-exact test or a
# regenerated syrupy snapshot flips the whole file in the diff.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` is the same rule tests/conftest.py writes into every fixture git repo it
# creates, so the fixtures and the real repository now agree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never normalized. None are tracked today; listed so adding one cannot corrupt it.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.whl binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
